Package: vpn-gate
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Recommends: iproute2, libnotify-bin
Maintainer: ViKuzmin <96813456+ViKuzmin@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ViKuzmin/vpn-gate
Description: Launch-time VPN gate for Linux apps — CLI installer + GTK4 GUI
 VPN Gate wraps any Linux application so it refuses to start unless a
 configured VPN network interface is up. The check happens at launch
 time: the wrapper either execs the real binary transparently or blocks
 it and logs the attempt. Works with any VPN client (WireGuard, Amnezia,
 OpenVPN, Tailscale, ...) — just point it at the right interface name.
 .
 Includes two tools:
  - vpn-gate-install: bash CLI to install/remove the gate for an app
  - vpn-gate-ui: GTK4/libadwaita GUI to manage protected apps, see
    live VPN status and review a log of blocked launch attempts
